| actual assigned call | actual middle | actual component | discovery |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0 | 0 | 0 | component start |
| 1 | 1 | 0 | call 0 via output |
| 2 | 0 | 0 | call 1 via input |

Actual original-order routes [0, 1, 0]; feasible certificate true.
\image(figures/switch_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual first assignments on a hand-checkable three-call bipartite path.)
\alttext(Calls sharing an endpoint alternate middles; feasibility is checked independently of the particular color orientation.)

> Retain the original four-cycle

The original calls are(0,0),(0,1),(1,1),(1,0). Native routing returns0,1,0,1 in
this original call order. BFS discovery order differs: it reaches calls through
incident lists, rather than simply processing each listed call once in sequence.
The table records that actual order. In the diagram, each colored two-link route
passes through its actual middle node. Wire crossings in this drawing are not
shared network links.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/switch_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nonblocking_switch.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto calls = dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_demo_calls();
    auto t = dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_trace(2, 2, calls);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {
        d.node("i" + std::to_string(i), {0., -5. * i},
               std::format("Input group {}", i));
        d.node("o" + std::to_string(i), {14., -5. * i},
               std::format("Output group {}", i));
        d.node("m" + std::to_string(i), {7., 3. - 11. * i},
               std::format("Middle {}", i));
    }
    std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{36, 105, 172}, {192, 59, 50}};
    for (std::size_t e = 0; e < calls.size(); ++e) {
        auto[u, v] = calls[e];
        auto middle = t.analysis.routes[e];
        dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;
        stroke.color = colors[middle];
        d.link("i" + std::to_string(u), "m" + std::to_string(middle),
               std::format("call {}", e), stroke);
        d.link("m" + std::to_string(middle), "o" + std::to_string(v), "", stroke);
    }
    std::print("| actual discovery position | original call ID | actual middle |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.assignments.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, t.assignments[i].call,
                   t.assignments[i].middle);
    std::print("\nOriginal-order routes {}; native feasible certificate {}.\n",
               t.analysis.routes,
               dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_feasible(2, 2, calls,
                                                           t.analysis.routes));
    d.save_svg("build/switch_original.svg");
}
```
