> Actual incidence reads and the linear bound

Each call is dequeued exactly once. At its two endpoints the producer scans both
incidence lists, including the call itself. Its actual candidate reads are
degree(input)+degree(output), at most four because both degrees are at most two.
Summing gives at most4C reads. Equality holds for the cycle family, including
two parallel calls when there is only one input/output group. The next native
fixture retains the original ordering when groups=2 and extends it to larger
cycles.

The complete O(I+O+C) work and storage bound also includes allocating/validating
all input and output group lists, which these selected traversal counters do not
measure. The graph proof ensures propagation does not encounter a conflicting
parity under the admitted domain. It does not remove the cost of complete input
checks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/switch_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nonblocking_switch.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> calls, reads, bound;
    std::print("| input/output groups each | actual calls | actual queue pops | actual incidence reads | " "feasible |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}) {
        auto c = dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_cycle_calls(n);
        auto r = dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_analyze(n, n, c);
        calls.push_back(c.size());
        reads.push_back(r.incidence_reads);
        bound.push_back(4 * c.size());
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, c.size(), r.queue_pops,
                   r.incidence_reads,
                   dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_feasible(n, n, c, r.routes));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(calls, bound, "4C bound", {192, 59, 50}).points(calls, reads,
                                                            "actual reads",
                                                            {36, 105, 172}, 5).title("Two-middle cycles: actual incidence reads").x_label("actual call count C").y_label("candidate incidence reads").save_svg("build/switch_work.svg");
}
```
