> Disconnected, parallel and empty controls

Disconnected components start independently at zero; an isolated call has no
color constraint from another call. The parallel-call control is a valid
two-edge cycle in a multigraph, and it uses both middles. Empty calls with zero
groups return an empty feasible routing. The table and chart compare actual
component counts rather than treating them as graph dimensions or physical
switch counts.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/switch_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/nonblocking_switch.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    using Calls = std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t, std::size_t>>;
    struct Case {
        std::string name;
        std::size_t groups;
        Calls calls;
    };
    std::vector<Case> cases{{"empty", 0, {}},
                            {"path", 2, {{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}}},
                            {"parallel", 1, {{0, 0}, {0, 0}}},
                            {"matching", 3, {{0, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 2}}}};
    std::vector<std::string> labels;
    std::vector<double> components;
    std::print("| control | actual routes | actual components | actual candidate reads | feasible |\n| --- " "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &c : cases) {
        auto r =
            dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_analyze(c.groups, c.groups,
                                                       c.calls);
        labels.push_back(c.name);
        components.push_back(r.components);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", c.name, r.routes,
                   r.components, r.incidence_reads,
                   dm::algorithms::nonblocking_switch_feasible(c.groups,
                                                               c.groups,
                                                               c.calls, r.routes));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(components, labels, "components");
    p.title("Actual call components: empty, path and multigraph controls").x_label("admitted call graph").y_label("components containing calls").save_svg("build/switch_controls.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| control | actual routes | actual components | actual candidate reads | feasible |
| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| empty | [] | 0 | 0 | true |
| path | [0, 1, 0] | 1 | 10 | true |
| parallel | [0, 1] | 1 | 8 | true |
| matching | [0, 0, 0] | 3 | 6 | true |
\image(figures/switch_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual component counts for admitted empty, path, parallel and disconnected call graphs.)
\alttext(The native certificate checks actual link conflicts, including valid independent color flips.)

> Complete contracts and capture policies

Every endpoint is checked against the original group counts before resource
policies. Complete group-count/container geometry is checked before dense
incidence allocation. Analyzed and traced calls default to1000000 total groups
and1000000 calls; ordinary routing disables those optional caps. Degrees are
checked before any color assignment. A degree above two or an out-of-range
endpoint throws rather than returning an incomplete routing.

After incidence validation, the exact complete logical trace size is known:2
group-count scalars,2C endpoint IDs,C output colors,C actual assignment records
and every actual incidence candidate record, totaling2+4C+reads. Its separate
default1000000-unit quota is checked before copying history or coloring; zero
disables each policy. Returned histories own their inputs and actual decisions.
These units count logical records rather than bytes or peak process memory.

The alternating-path/even-cycle proof above establishes feasibility for this
restricted model directly. The original four-cycle result is retained, while the
report distinguishes actual traversal order, selectable color orientation and a
verified route certificate from broader claims about arbitrary nonblocking
network designs.

